{"term":"qualify","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4af9832a7abffa8dce","definition":"To describe or characterize something by listing its qualities.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["disqualify","unqualify"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["disqualify","misqualify","nonqualifying","outqualify","overqualify","postqualifying","prequalify","qualifiability","qualifiable","qualified","qualifier","qualifying","qualifyingly","qualify out","requalify","self-qualify","self-qualifying","subqualify","unqualify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a09b485609c5cab24b","definition":"To successfully fall under some category or description by meeting requisite conditions.","example":"Descartes's methodism with its regulative criterion leads him to explicitly deny that accidentally true belief qualifies as knowledge.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["disqualify","unqualify"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["disqualify","misqualify","nonqualifying","outqualify","overqualify","postqualifying","prequalify","qualifiability","qualifiable","qualified","qualifier","qualifying","qualifyingly","qualify out","requalify","self-qualify","self-qualifying","subqualify","unqualify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dea0817a07b1f23839","definition":"To make someone competent or eligible for some position or task.","example":"They usually spoke of this connection as a longing for the purer life of Attic civilization, but that was a delusion which even they recognized — the position of slaves and women hardly qualified Classical antiquity as an ideal of freedom.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["disqualify","unqualify"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["disqualify","misqualify","nonqualifying","outqualify","overqualify","postqualifying","prequalify","qualifiability","qualifiable","qualified","qualifier","qualifying","qualifyingly","qualify out","requalify","self-qualify","self-qualifying","subqualify","unqualify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ef756e381dd5a9166a","definition":"To become competent or eligible for some position or task.","example":"He had qualified himself for municipal office by taking the oaths to the sovereigns in possession.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["disqualify","unqualify"],"collocations":[],"usage":"reflexive","register":"intransitive, reflexive","wordFamily":["disqualify","misqualify","nonqualifying","outqualify","overqualify","postqualifying","prequalify","qualifiability","qualifiable","qualified","qualifier","qualifying","qualifyingly","qualify out","requalify","self-qualify","self-qualifying","subqualify","unqualify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:94d7388217298234c9","definition":"To certify or license someone for something.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["disqualify","unqualify"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["disqualify","misqualify","nonqualifying","outqualify","overqualify","postqualifying","prequalify","qualifiability","qualifiable","qualified","qualifier","qualifying","qualifyingly","qualify out","requalify","self-qualify","self-qualifying","subqualify","unqualify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c7757427fc4183593d","definition":"To modify, limit, restrict or moderate something; especially to add conditions or requirements for an assertion to be true.","example":"O! never say that I was false of heart,\nThough absence seem'd my flame to qualify","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["disqualify","unqualify"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["disqualify","misqualify","nonqualifying","outqualify","overqualify","postqualifying","prequalify","qualifiability","qualifiable","qualified","qualifier","qualifying","qualifyingly","qualify out","requalify","self-qualify","self-qualifying","subqualify","unqualify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5cec71581462877a30","definition":"To mitigate, alleviate (something); to make less disagreeable.","example":"he balmes and herbes thereto applyde, / And euermore with mighty spels them charmd, / That in short space he has them qualifyde, / And him restor'd to health, that would haue algates dyde.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["disqualify","unqualify"],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["disqualify","misqualify","nonqualifying","outqualify","overqualify","postqualifying","prequalify","qualifiability","qualifiable","qualified","qualifier","qualifying","qualifyingly","qualify out","requalify","self-qualify","self-qualifying","subqualify","unqualify"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f2aa619641612e183f","definition":"To compete successfully in some stage of a competition and become eligible for the next stage.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":